>**Things to work on**<
The biggest note I got was don't control. Let the gifts unfold naturally. Otherwise it will be forced and nobody wants that. Give yourself the gift. Surrender yourself to the scene. Preload want / backstory. Be affected by everything

Make the scenes dynamic. Make the active choice. Don't say you are going to do something just do it. Don't talk about what happened in the past. Do it now. Less talking more doing

Frustrate the negative wants or low status. Let's see the positive wants In the most ridiculous ways  Show don't tell

[[beat game]]
location
Relationship
Character
Energy
Focus on one and the scene will follow

Listen by parroting
===
>** Journal **<


2025-09-10 I surrender control. I set myself up for the joke. They weren't the best scenes but I enjoyed them so much more than focusing on doing amazing improv. 

Things to work on: someone saying something tangential to the game takes me out of the moment for a second. I need to move around stage more. figure out how to project voices

Things I did great: object work. Letting myself be affected. 

2025-11-02


